invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: multiple_select tests the mask and moves on when the multiple is
  not the digit's, so the scan reads and writes one multiple of eight,
  and which one is four bits of the private scalar on the control path
  and in the cache. The values stay right, so the vectors, the
  equivalence binary and the proofs all pass; only the count of what the
  compiler emits sees it. The pinned clang emits one more conditional
  branch for p256_wide_mul.c on both 64-bit specs, above the file's
  ceiling.

--- old
        uint64_t mask = equal_mask(j, index);
        fe_keep(&o->x, &row[j].x, mask);
        fe_keep(&o->y, &row[j].y, mask);
        fe_keep(&o->z, &row[j].z, mask);
--- new
        uint64_t mask = equal_mask(j, index);
        if (mask == 0) {
            continue;
        }
        fe_keep(&o->x, &row[j].x, mask);
        fe_keep(&o->y, &row[j].y, mask);
        fe_keep(&o->z, &row[j].z, mask);
